  "status_text": "The drops forced by the rules now tell us exactly which flip budgets can work. Lean checked partial answer tables. A forced drop goes from a required one to a required zero for the same answer as switches only turn on. Successive drops may share endpoints. With no cap on other gates, r NOTs work exactly when no chain has 2 to the r drops. If every chain has at most d drops and d is below that threshold, at most (n+2)S+L+5d AND or OR gates suffice too, for n inputs, S labeled settings and L required ones. Gates read at most two earlier wires, with free constants (L-lib-1228).",
